# The pieces a bare boolean cannot say. A test is a constant whose name begins
# `test_`, and `==` is the assertion — nothing here adds a second way to write
# a test that can already be written.
#
# Every tested package's errs are foreign to this hako, so these arms are
# licensed by the rules as they stand: no builtin, no file gating, no
# exemption.
pub fn failed? (err _)
  true

pub fn failed? _
  false

# Asserting WHICH failure. The err is rescued here, where the raiser is
# foreign, and the caller receives the bare reason record — a value a licensed
# party has already separated from the failure, so the tested package may read
# its own reason without matching its own err.
#
# A non-failure answers false, so a test that expected a failure and got a
# value fails rather than passing quietly.
pub fn when_failed (err reason) k
  k reason

pub fn when_failed _ _
  false
